{"candidates":[{"content":"The adjudication-ritual flag (§11.3) is sustained because the verdict-shape imposes an impossible joint requirement: it mandates that every surviving candidate satisfy both soundness and frontier-relevance simultaneously, a condition that cannot be reliably met under finite evidence, causing persistent failure.","typicality":0.85,"neighbours":["SRC_003","SRC_004"]},{"content":"The flag is sustained by design as a stabilizing negative-feedback loop that prevents premature closure; the ritual deliberately maintains a high adjudicatory bar so that the system avoids settling on under-supported conjectures.","typicality":0.75,"neighbours":["SRC_005"]},{"content":"The §11.3 flag persists because of a type confusion in the critic harness: it conflates a meta-level judgment (the verdict is sound and relevant) with an object-level judgment (the candidate itself is sound and relevant), causing the ritual to reject verdicts for properties they only describe.","typicality":0.65,"neighbours":["SRC_006","SRC_007"]},{"content":"The flag is an artifact of temporal misalignment between two critic phases: 'sound and relevant' affirmations are registered before the frontier-exclusion check completes, so the system records both success and failure for the same candidate, sustaining a spurious flag.","typicality":0.6,"neighbours":["SRC_008","SRC_006"]},{"content":"The flag is sustained because the two critics, frontier-claim-honest and frontier-above-floor, are redundant probes of the same latent quality; their near-collinear signals create a systematic covariance that the harness misreads as independent disagreement, blocking convergence.","typicality":0.55,"neighbours":["SRC_004"]},{"content":"The flag persists because the critics are adversarial validators operating under a covering principle of mutual exclusion at the frontier: any candidate that survives the soundness critic is necessarily pushed below the frontier by the relevance critic, making sustained failure structural rather than accidental.","typicality":0.7,"neighbours":["SRC_007","SRC_003"]}]}